{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 1, "cache": "cold", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 20.61, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:14.789Z", "turn_id": "turn_4cc58668", "session_id": "fca98d90c05a", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 6, "duration_ms": 19137, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.04701686, "usage": {"input_tokens": 14, "output_tokens": 1229, "cache_read_input_tokens": 43971, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 10411}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "I analysed a 600 \u00d7 600 m area around Chalmers (EPSG:3006: 319200\u2013319800 E, 6397700\u20136398300 N). I used a 2 m ground-surface elevation model built from about 745,000 lidar points.\n\n**Elevation**\n- The range is 41.4\u201386.9 m, with a mean of 61.4 m and a median of 62.2 m.\n- 90% of the terrain lies between 46.5 and 75.0 m, so the area has about 40 m of relief overall.\n\n**Slope**\nThe tool doesn't state units. I'm assuming radians, because the aspect output spans \u00b1\u03c0.\n\n| Statistic | Radians | Degrees |\n|---|---|---|\n| Median | 0.074 | ~4.2\u00b0 |\n| Mean | 0.154 | ~8.8\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | 0.553 | ~31.7\u00b0 |\n| Max | 1.29 | ~74\u00b0 |\n\n- Most of the terrain is gentle. Half of it is under about 4\u00b0.\n- The mean is about twice the median, so a minority of cells are much steeper. About 5% exceed 30\u00b0, which would be rock cuts, embankments and steep hillsides.\n- Aspect was computed, but its values are spread across all directions (\u00b1\u03c0). There is no dominant slope direction in the summary.\n\nThe slope and aspect results are summary statistics only. They don't say where the steep or flat cells are, so I can't name specific locations. The 3D render I made shows the terrain mesh (43\u201383 m, 8,490 triangles), not the slope field. It shows the terrain shape only.\n\nI can rerun this over a smaller area, or export the slope raster as a TIFF or CSV for mapping.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:24:55.614Z", "turn_id": "turn_4cc58668", "session_id": "fca98d90c05a", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.004, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:00.791Z", "turn_id": "turn_4cc58668", "session_id": "fca98d90c05a", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "64a3a011e993bc8b", "seconds": 3.881, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_7e730214"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:02.220Z", "turn_id": "turn_4cc58668", "session_id": "fca98d90c05a", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "cb2347c48e899864", "seconds": 0.072, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_30b70315"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:04.150Z", "turn_id": "turn_4cc58668", "session_id": "fca98d90c05a", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_surface_mesh", "params_hash": "4f8c58d03191bb0a", "seconds": 0.243, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_b6a966ec"], "ca