campus areas.\n- **Steep tail:** the top 5% of cells are steeper than about 32\u00b0. These probably include rock outcrops, embankments and cut slopes, since the Chalmers hillsides are rocky. The statistics don't say where these cells are.\n- **Extreme values:** the maximum of about 74\u00b0 is likely a DEM artifact, such as the edge of a retaining wall or a building. I'd treat it with caution.\n- **Aspect:** it spans the full \u2212\u03c0 to \u03c0 range with a median of about \u22120.2 rad. The slopes face many directions, with no single dominant direction.\n\nI can't say where the steep or flat areas are, because the tools returned only summary statistics for slope and aspect. I can export the slope raster as a GeoTIFF or CSV for GIS use. I can also rerun at a finer cell size (for example 1 m) or on a smaller area.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:37.622Z", "turn_id": "turn_add01b5c", "session_id": "4125160a3ed9", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.002, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:38.924Z", "turn_id": "turn_add01b5c", "session_id": "4125160a3ed9", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "64a3a011e993bc8b", "seconds": 0.077, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_ec2d9b0e"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:40.323Z", "turn_id": "turn_add01b5c", "session_id": "4125160a3ed9", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "a18ff0a4411474c1", "seconds": 0.086, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_d624a46a"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d5182