{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 2, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 11.35, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:02.201Z", "turn_id": "turn_504c6665", "session_id": "4bd233d6347d", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 3, "duration_ms": 11149, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.01602359, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1025, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24384, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 745}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "I couldn't download the 5 km \u00d7 5 km area (25 km\u00b2). The point cloud download is limited to 10 km\u00b2 per request, because LiDAR data at that size needs several GB of memory. I haven't downloaded anything yet.\n\nThe geocoder also matched \"Central Gothenburg\" to G\u00f6teborgs Central station. I centered the 5 km box there, at about E 319676, N 6400379 (EPSG:3006).\n\nHere are the options:\n\n1. **One 3 km \u00d7 3 km tile (9 km\u00b2) around the station.** This is a single download and the quickest.\n2. **Split the 5 km area into smaller tiles.** Nine tiles would be about 1.7 km each, and four would be 2.5 km each (6.25 km\u00b2 per tile). I'd download them one by one, and each stays under the limit. The tiles would be separate point clouds, not one merged object.\n3. **A different center or a narrower focus.** For example, only the city core, Haga, or Lindholmen.\n\nWhich would you like? If you don't mind, I'll start with option 1 and add tiles after.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:53.033Z", "turn_id": "turn_504c6665", "session_id": "4bd233d6347d", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "862c813d77e68dca", "seconds": 0.072, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:25:55.710Z", "turn_id": "turn_504c6665", "session_id": "4bd233d6347d", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "fd420760f0e51296", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": false, "error": "Refused", "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}
{"question_id": "q03-terrain-slope", "run": 3, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 14.23, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:16.437Z", "turn_id": "turn_9d501799", "session_id": "61317b5b0aad", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "render_object"], "num_turns": 6, "duration_ms": 13885, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.026455, "usage": {"input_tokens": 14, "output_tokens": 1350, "cache_read_input_tokens": 52195, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2121}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 1, "files": 0, "answer": "Chalmers (600 \u00d7 600 m, 2 m DEM) is mostly flat, with a steep hill edge on part of the area.\n\n**Terrain elevation (ground points)**\n- Range: 41.4\u201386.9 m\n- Mean: 61.4 m\n- 5th\u201395th percentile: 46.5\u201375.0 m\n\n**Slope**\n\nThe tool's slope values look like radians (maximum 1.29, aspect from \u2212\u03c0 to \u03c0). I converted them to degrees myself.\n\n| Statistic | Slope |\n|---|---|\n| Median | about 4.2\u00b0 |\n| Mean | about 8.8\u00b0 |\n| 5th percentile | about 0.4\u00b0 |\n| 95th percentile | about 31.7\u00b0 |\n| Maximum | about 74\u00b0 |\n\n- **Overall:** The median is far below the mean, so most cells are gentle. The slope distribution is skewed by a minority of steep cells.\n- **Steep cells:** About 5% of cells are steeper than roughly 32\u00b0. The very steepest cells, up to about 74\u00b0, may be rock cuts or retaining walls, or artefacts of the 2 m raster.\n- **Height difference:** The ground rises about 45 m across the area. That is a substantial hill, so slope matters for drainage, accessibility and building foundations.\n- **Aspect:** It was computed, but the summary statistics are not meaningful for direction. The results give no spatial breakdown, so I can't say which slopes face which way.\n\nI rendered a 3D terrain mesh of the area, but it shows only the elevation surface. It doesn't show the slope field, so I can't say where the steep parts are from these results.\n\nI can also run a finer 1 m DEM, build a mesh that includes the buildings, or run a heat or air-quality simulation on this area.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:03.581Z", "turn_id": "turn_9d501799", "session_id": "61317b5b0aad", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "ad5faefbe482eb39", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:04.846Z", "turn_id": "turn_9d501799", "session_id": "61317b5b0aad", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "64a3a011e993bc8b", "seconds": 0.04, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_d383bf17"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:06.094Z", "turn_id": "turn_9d501799", "session_id": "61317b5b0aad", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.build_terrain_raster", "params_hash": "2c1da88c78c145f6", "seconds": 0.076, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": ["obj_45a19066"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:07.838Z", "turn_id": "turn_9d501799", "session_id": "61317b5b0aad", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "builder.raster.slope_aspect", "params_hash": "73838ca6e8