{"question_id": "q09-too-large", "run": 3, "cache": "warm", "status": "ok", "error": null, "latency_s": 32.73, "provenance": {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:49.170Z", "turn_id": "turn_a9e34117", "session_id": "0138e6cc37b7", "subject": "anonymous", "model": "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5", "models_used": ["eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"], "prompt_version": "a9f7e88fc432", "memory_context": false, "sdk": "pydantic-ai-slim 2.54.0", "tools_called": ["geocode", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation", "run_operation"], "num_turns": 4, "duration_ms": 32469, "duration_api_ms": null, "total_cost_usd": 0.03242305, "usage": {"input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1826, "cache_read_input_tokens": 33230, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3149}, "is_error": false, "retried_fresh": false, "refused": false, "error": null, "http_status": null, "runtime": "pydantic-ai", "provider": "bedrock", "cost_source": "genai-prices 0.1.13 (regional.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5)"}, "images": 0, "files": 0, "answer": "The geocoder matched the central station area and returned a box of about 0.6 \u00d7 1.1 km, so it ignored the radius. I'll use its center point and build a 5 \u00d7 5 km box around it.The tool caps a single download at 10 km\u00b2, and 5 \u00d7 5 km is 25 km\u00b2. I'll split the area into four 2.5 km tiles, each 6.25 km\u00b2.I downloaded the point cloud for central Gothenburg as four tiles, about 47.8 million points in total. They cover a 5 \u00d7 5 km square (25 km\u00b2) centered on G\u00f6teborgs central station (EPSG:3006: 319676, 6400380).\n\nI split it because the tool allows only 10 km\u00b2 per download. The tiles are separate objects, and I haven't merged them.\n\n| Tile | Object ref | Points | Elevation range (m) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SW | `obj_9f651fd3` | 12.6 M | \u2212133 to 115 |\n| SE | `obj_8c433622` | 14.0 M | \u221297 to 568 |\n| NW | `obj_906d1665` | 10.8 M | \u2212228 to 314 |\n| NE | `obj_a3d0eb95` | 10.4 M | \u2212334 to 503 |\n\n- **Classifications:** Each tile contains the same classes:\n  - ground (2)\n  - unclassified (1)\n  - low points/noise (7)\n  - water (9)\n  - bridge (17)\n  - high noise (18)\n- **Outliers:** The extreme elevation values, such as \u2212334 m and +568 m, are almost certainly noise. I downloaded with `remove_outliers=false`, so they are still in the data. Filtering out classes 7 and 18, or re-downloading with outlier removal, would clean them up.\n\nI can build a terrain mesh or DEM for each tile or filter the noise. A 5 km area at this density is heavy, so I'd suggest a coarse cell size (5\u201310 m) for a DEM or mesh. I haven't rendered anything yet because the point clouds are too dense to draw.", "operations": [{"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:18.748Z", "turn_id": "turn_a9e34117", "session_id": "0138e6cc37b7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "geocode", "operation": null, "params_hash": "862c813d77e68dca", "seconds": 0.068, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:21.742Z", "turn_id": "turn_a9e34117", "session_id": "0138e6cc37b7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "fd420760f0e51296", "seconds": 0.001, "ok": false, "error": "Refused", "cache_hit": false, "object_refs": [], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:27.455Z", "turn_id": "turn_a9e34117", "session_id": "0138e6cc37b7", "subject": "anonymous", "tool": "run_operation", "operation": "datasets.point_cloud", "params_hash": "25331dcadaf3148e", "seconds": 0.898, "ok": true, "error": null, "cache_hit": true, "object_refs": ["obj_9f651fd3"], "catalogue": {"core_commit": "a78df16e9c86b349ba3a67551d518223b7897443", "operations": 133}}, {"at": "2026-10-19T23:26:34.727Z", "turn_id": "turn_a9e34117", "session_id": "0138e6cc37b7", "subject": "anonymo